WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.617
When speaking or using a touchscreen is difficult. a simple message
can be hard to express.

2
00:00:05.617 --> 00:00:12.638
CareSwitch explores a low cost way to choose and speak prepared
messages using voluntary head movement and an ordinary webcam.

3
00:00:12.638 --> 00:00:16.148
This walkthrough shows real app screenshots in mouse practice mode.

4
00:00:16.148 --> 00:00:18.605
It does not demonstrate live head tracking.

5
00:00:20.105 --> 00:00:26.097
The intended user can voluntarily and comfortably move their head.
with a helper for setup if needed.

6
00:00:26.097 --> 00:00:31.384
The camera mode uses the pretrained MediaPipe face landmark model in a
local browser worker.

7
00:00:31.384 --> 00:00:33.851
Five setup steps establish the movement range.

8
00:00:33.851 --> 00:00:37.728
Filtering. smoothing and a speed limit steady the in app pointer.

9
00:00:37.728 --> 00:00:40.548
This is head control. not eye gaze tracking.

10
00:00:42.048 --> 00:00:45.780
Here is an actual selection of I need a break.

11
00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:48.019
Choosing the card creates a draft.

12
00:00:48.019 --> 00:00:49.511
Nothing is spoken yet.

13
00:00:49.511 --> 00:00:52.496
The user reviews the exact text before confirming.

14
00:00:52.496 --> 00:00:54.362
Cancel discards a wrong draft.

15
00:00:54.362 --> 00:01:01.079
In head control mode. moving away between selection and confirmation
helps prevent one hold from triggering both actions.

16
00:01:02.579 --> 00:01:07.695
After Confirm. the chosen message appears as the final message and
speech is attempted.

17
00:01:07.695 --> 00:01:11.349
If audio is blocked or unavailable. the text remains visible.

18
00:01:11.349 --> 00:01:13.176
Read again allows another attempt.

19
00:01:13.176 --> 00:01:17.561
CareSwitch does not generate medical advice or decide what the user
means.

20
00:01:17.561 --> 00:01:20.485
It reads the message the user has chosen.

21
00:01:21.985 --> 00:01:26.661
Prepared messages cover English. Urdu. Arabic. Hindi. Spanish. French.
German and Chinese.

22
00:01:26.661 --> 00:01:30.168
A matching local device voice is used when available.

23
00:01:30.168 --> 00:01:39.909
A bundled free eSpeak engine provides a fallback for all eight
choices. with no paid speech API and no text sent to a speech service.

24
00:01:39.909 --> 00:01:41.468
The voice is synthetic.

25
00:01:41.468 --> 00:01:43.806
Pronunciation still needs fluent speaker feedback.

26
00:01:45.306 --> 00:01:49.677
Settings adjust hold time. movement sensitivity. pointer smoothing and
direction.

27
00:01:49.677 --> 00:01:53.612
The free built in voice can be selected directly.

28
00:01:53.612 --> 00:01:57.983
Missing faces. multiple faces or stale tracking stop dwell selection.

29
00:01:57.983 --> 00:02:04.977
These controls reduce accidental activation. but do not establish
clinical safety or suitability for every user.

30
00:02:06.477 --> 00:02:10.206
The six phrases can be edited in the selected language.

31
00:02:10.206 --> 00:02:16.173
Mouse. keyboard and touch alternatives let a helper or user try the
board without a camera.

32
00:02:16.173 --> 00:02:18.784
The small screen layout keeps messages readable.

33
00:02:18.784 --> 00:02:21.022
The setup interface is currently English.

34
00:02:21.022 --> 00:02:24.751
Physical phone performance and intended user comfort still need
testing.

35
00:02:26.251 --> 00:02:30.091
Camera frames are not recorded or uploaded by the app.

36
00:02:30.091 --> 00:02:32.011
There is no patient database.

37
00:02:32.011 --> 00:02:37.771
The caregiver card speaks a request to a nearby listener; it does not
contact anyone.

38
00:02:37.771 --> 00:02:40.459
AI tools helped build this student prototype.

39
00:02:40.459 --> 00:02:42.763
It has not been clinically validated.

40
00:02:42.763 --> 00:02:46.987
The next step is feedback from intended users and accessibility
specialists.

41
00:02:46.987 --> 00:02:47.755
Your movement.

42
00:02:47.755 --> 00:02:48.523
Your message.
